## 8. Phase-by-Phase Setup & Troubleshooting

### Phase 1: Memory Optimization & Timeout Fixes
If the dashboard shows *"Wazuh dashboard server is not ready yet"*, the database (OpenSearch/Indexer) crashed due to low host RAM.

#### Fix 1: Restrict Java Heap Memory to 1GB
Open JVM options file:
```bash
sudo nano /etc/wazuh-indexer/jvm.options

```

Change memory allocations to:

```text
-Xms1g
-Xmx1g

```

#### Fix 2: Extend Startup Timeout (For Slower HDDs)

Open startup override file:

```bash
sudo nano /etc/systemd/system/wazuh-indexer.service.d/startup-timeout.conf

```

Add timeout value:

```text
[Service]
TimeoutStartSec=1200

```

Apply rules and enable auto-start on boot:

```bash
sudo systemctl daemon-reload
sudo systemctl enable wazuh-indexer wazuh-manager wazuh-dashboard
sudo reboot

```

---

### Phase 2: Password & OpenSearch Security Index Reset

If `admin`/`admin` credentials return an *Invalid Username or Password* error, force sync the security index and reset passwords:

```bash
sudo su

# Force Sync OpenSearch / Wazuh Security Index
/usr/share/wazuh-indexer/plugins/opensearch-security/tools/securityadmin.sh \
-cd /etc/wazuh-indexer/opensearch-security/ \
-icl -nhnv \
-cacert /etc/wazuh-indexer/certs/root-ca.pem \
-cert /etc/wazuh-indexer/certs/admin.pem \
-key /etc/wazuh-indexer/certs/admin-key.pem

# Reset Admin Password
/usr/share/wazuh-indexer/plugins/opensearch-security/tools/wazuh-passwords-tool.sh -u admin -p "Secret123@"

# Restart Services
systemctl restart wazuh-indexer wazuh-dashboard

```

